      "entryId": "ezr-7-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Artaxerxes I issues the comprehensive decree to Ezra granting full authority to restore and rebuild Jerusalem, appointing magistrates and restoring the laws of God. This decree in 457 BC (the autumn of Artaxerxes' 7th regnal year) marks the undeniable chronological starting point for both the 70 weeks of Daniel 9:25 and the 2,300 days of Daniel 8:14. First principle: biblical prophecy is rooted in verifiable history; the exact dating of the Messiah's first advent confirms the timeline for the cleansing of the heavenly sanctuary.",
      "density": 3.9857,
      "words": 84,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 33,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Daniel 9:25",
          "Daniel 8:14"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "ezr-9-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Mercy before Persian kings: reviving, house-raising, a wall in Judah. First principle: grace gives reviving and repair — the forsaken people rebuilt with a wall and a worship.",
